subgraph Phase46["Phase 46 — Bookmarks Backend Integration (Implemented)"]

Q1["BookmarkService — single Firestore writer for users/{uid}/bookmarks; deterministic bookmarkId = '${type.name}_${itemId}'; idempotent toggle (merge write)"]
Q2["BookmarkService.add(uid, model) → firestore.collection(users/{uid}/bookmarks).doc(id).set(model.toJson(), SetOptions(merge: true)) — preserves existing fields while updatedAtIso propagates"]
Q3["BookmarkService.remove(uid, type, itemId) + removeById(uid, id) → reads doc.get() then ref.delete(); returns true when the doc existed, false when missing"]
Q4["BookmarkService.clearAll(uid) → WriteBatch deletes every doc in users/{uid}/bookmarks; returns the count actually removed"]
Q5["BookmarkService.snapshot(uid) — one-shot read used by BookmarkRepositoryImpl.sync() to seed the local cache on pull-to-refresh"]
Q6["BookmarkService.watch(uid) — CollectionReference.snapshots() stream; emits on every Firestore mutation so the controller + widget tree refresh without manual refresh"]
Q7["BookmarkService.userBookmarksStreamProvider — StreamProvider.autoDispose<List<BookmarkModel>>; auth-aware (empty uid returns empty list); the canonical realtime source"]
Q8["BookmarkEntity — adequate as-is; no schema migration required (title, subtitle, thumbnailIconKey, sourceFeature, tags, routeName, routeParams all preserved)"]
Q9["BookmarkItemType — enum { question, lesson, aiResponse, note }; drives the destination widget (question detail, lesson reader, AI hint, note editor) and the icon shown next to each tile"]
Q10["BookmarkModel — JSON round-trip; createdAtIso / updatedAtIso encoded as ISO strings; deterministic id derived from (itemType, itemId)"]
Q11["BookmarkLocalDataSource — in-memory mirror; filter / sort / search / paginate over the cached rows; writeAll emits changes for widget refresh"]
Q12["BookmarkRemoteDataSource — replaces historic UnimplementedError stub; pull() delegates to BookmarkService.snapshot(uid); push() is a no-op reconcile (BookmarkService is the only writer); upsert(model) + removeById(id) + remove(type, itemId) + clearAll() route to BookmarkService"]
Q13["BookmarkRepositoryImpl — remote-first (preferRemote = true); remoteStreamFactory closure wires the realtime Firestore stream into the local cache; mutations write through to BookmarkService"]
Q14["addBookmark writes local cache then forwards to BookmarkService.upsert; removeBookmark deletes locally then forwards to BookmarkService.removeById; clearAll wipes local cache then forwards to BookmarkService.clearAll"]
Q15["sync() calls BookmarkRemoteDataSource.pull() (delegates to BookmarkService.snapshot); realtime subscription also mirrors the same data so widgets refresh without explicit refresh"]
Q16["bookmarkCurrentUidProvider — resolves auth.user.id; empty string for guests (Firestore writes skipped)"]
Q17["bookmarkRepositoryProvider — composes BookmarkLocalDataSource + BookmarkRemoteDataSource (with realtime stream factory) + preferRemote = true; ref.onDispose cancels the remote subscription"]
Q18["BookmarkController — ref.listen on userBookmarksStreamProvider; every Firestore snapshot mirrors into the local datasource + re-hydrates BookmarksViewState.items"]
Q19["Toggle flow: BookmarkActionButton → BookmarkController.toggle(entity) → ToggleBookmark usecase → BookmarkRepositoryImpl.addBookmark or removeBookmark (via findBookmarkId)"]
Q20["Guest guard — empty uid short-circuits every BookmarkService method; local cache still mirrors in-session actions so the UI shows fresh state"]
Q21["Idempotency — deterministic doc id '${type.name}_${itemId}' ensures re-toggling the same item collapses into the same Firestore doc (no duplicate rows, no merge conflicts across devices)"]
Q22["Best-effort writes — BookmarkService.add / remove / clearAll catch all errors and debugPrint + return safely; the local cache is the canonical UI mirror so the user never sees a failed toggle"]
Q23["FirestoreKeys.bookmarksSubcollection = 'bookmarks' — constant added under users/{uid}/* subcollection block"]
Q24["Realtime UI: device A toggles a bookmark → Firestore mutation → userBookmarksStreamProvider emits → BookmarkController re-hydrates → bookmarkIdsProvider recomputes → BookmarkActionButton re-renders on device B without polling"]
Q25["BookmarkActionButton — universal toggle shared by questions, lessons, AI responses, notes, search results, and bookmark tiles; derives bookmarked state from bookmarkIdsProvider (which reads bookmarkControllerProvider.items)"]
Q26["bookmarkIdsProvider — Provider<Set<String>> derived from bookmarkControllerProvider.items; key = '${type.name}:${itemId}'; BookmarkActionButton watches this set for instant fill-state updates"]

