subgraph Phase48["Phase 48 — Backend Notifications Integration (Implemented)"]

S1["NotificationService — single Firestore writer for users/{uid}/notifications + users/{uid}/fcm_tokens/{deviceId}; auto-generated doc ids; merge-write idempotency"]
S2["NotificationService.upsert(uid, model) → firestore.collection(users/{uid}/notifications).doc(id).set(model.toJson(), SetOptions(merge: true)); auto-stamps createdAtIso"]
S3["NotificationService.markAsRead(uid, notificationId) → merge update with {isRead: true}; returns true on success"]
S4["NotificationService.markAllAsRead(uid) → WriteBatch flips isRead on every unread doc; returns the count actually updated"]
S5["NotificationService.remove(uid, notificationId) → reads doc.get() then ref.delete(); returns true when the doc existed"]
S6["NotificationService.snapshot(uid) — one-shot read used by NotificationRepositoryImpl to seed the local cache"]
S7["NotificationService.watch(uid) — CollectionReference.snapshots() realtime stream; emits on every Firestore mutation so the controller + widget tree refresh without manual refresh"]
S8["NotificationService.registerToken(uid, deviceId, token, platform, metadata) → firestore.collection(users/{uid}/fcm_tokens).doc(deviceId).set({token, platform, registeredAtIso, lastSeenAtIso, metadata}, merge: true); supports multiple devices per user"]
S9["NotificationService.unregisterToken(uid, deviceId) — sign-out cleanup; reads doc.get() then ref.delete()"]
S10["NotificationService.watchTokens(uid) — realtime stream of every registered device token; used by the FCM bootstrap to detect token rotation events"]
S11["NotificationService.userNotificationsStreamProvider — StreamProvider.autoDispose<List<NotificationModel>>; auth-aware (empty uid returns empty list); the canonical realtime source"]
S12["NotificationType { reminder, mission, reward, announcement, system, aiSuggestion, subscription, dailyQuiz, streak, levelUp, xpEarned, coinReward, generic } + NotificationPriority { low, normal, high } — drive the icon, color, and Cloud Function selector on the backend"]
S13["NotificationEntity — extended with optional type / imageUrl / deepLink / priority / expiresAtIso / payload; every pre-Phase 48 constructor call site stays valid"]
S14["NotificationModel — JSON round-trip; new fields encoded by name and decoded with sensible defaults; copyWith preserves every existing call site"]
S15["NotificationLocalDataSource — in-memory mirror; readAll / writeAll; no per-row events (realtime stream is the source of truth)"]
S16["NotificationRemoteDataSource — replaces historic UnimplementedError stub; readAll delegates to NotificationService.snapshot(uid); upsert / markAsRead / markAllAsRead / remove route to NotificationService"]
S17["NotificationRepositoryImpl — remote-first (preferRemote = true); remoteStreamFactory closure wires the realtime Firestore stream into the local cache; mutations write through to NotificationService"]
S18["fetchAll / markAsRead / markAllAsRead / delete — write local cache then forward to NotificationRemoteDataSource; failures are best-effort and debugPrint-logged without surfacing to the user"]
S19["notificationCurrentUidProvider — resolves auth.user.id; empty string for guests (Firestore writes skipped)"]
S20["notificationRepositoryProvider — composes NotificationLocalDataSource + NotificationRemoteDataSource (with realtime stream factory) + preferRemote = true; ref.onDispose cancels the remote subscription"]
S21["NotificationController — ref.listen on userNotificationsStreamProvider; every Firestore snapshot mirrors into the local datasource + re-hydrates NotificationViewState.items"]
S22["notificationUnreadCountProvider — Provider<int> derived from NotificationController.items.where(!isRead).length; consumed by playground_screen and profile_screen for the badge count"]
S23["registerFcmTokenProvider / unregisterFcmTokenProvider — Provider<Future<bool> Function(...)> wrappers around NotificationService.registerToken / unregisterToken; consumed by FcmBootstrap"]
S24["FcmBootstrap — auth-aware FCM token-registration seam; FcmBootstrap.bind(ref, bootstrap) wires a ref.listen on authStateProvider that (re)registers the token on every sign-in; stub tokenSource / deviceIdSource return null / placeholder so the layer compiles before firebase_messaging is added"]
S25["SettingsService — Firestore writer for users/{uid}/settings/notification_preferences; saveNotificationPreferences(uid, model) → merge write; loadNotificationPreferences(uid) → one-shot read; watchNotificationPreferences(uid) → realtime stream; userNotificationPreferencesStreamProvider exposes the auth-aware stream"]
S26["SettingsRepositoryImpl — SettingsLocalDataSource is the UI mirror; SettingsService is the backend mirror for the notification-preferences slice; best-effort failure (logged) keeps the local cache canonical"]
S27["Settings provider — injects SettingsService + notificationCurrentUidProvider via SettingsRepositoryImpl; every saveSettings call also writes to users/{uid}/settings/notification_preferences"]
S28["Guest guard — empty uid short-circuits every NotificationService + SettingsService method; local cache still mirrors in-session actions so the UI shows fresh state; no Firestore writes happen for unauthenticated users"]
S29["Idempotency — auto-generated doc ids for ad-hoc writes; deterministic ids from Cloud Functions merge into the same Firestore doc across devices (no duplicate rows, no merge conflicts)"]
S30["Best-effort writes — NotificationService.upsert / markAsRead / markAllAsRead / remove / registerToken / unregisterToken catch all errors and debugPrint + return safely; the local cache is the canonical UI mirror so the user never sees a failed toggle"]
S31["FirestoreKeys.notificationsSubcollection = 'notifications' + fcmTokensSubcollection = 'fcm_tokens' + settingsSubcollection = 'settings' + notificationPreferencesDoc = 'notification_preferences' — constants added under users/{uid}/* subcollection block"]
S32["Realtime UI: Cloud Function sendPush / sendDailyReminder / sendTopicNotification writes a notification doc → userNotificationsStreamProvider emits → NotificationController re-hydrates → notificationUnreadCountProvider recomputes → playground + profile badges re-render without polling"]
S33["Deep linking — notification.routeName / deepLink survives a JSON round-trip; NotificationTile / router still consume the existing field; future iOS / Android intent parsing slots into the same payload"]
S34["Existing Cloud Functions — functions/src/notifications/{sendPush,sendDailyReminder,sendTopicNotification}.ts — target the same Firestore layout; backend engineers fill the implementations in a follow-up; the Flutter layer is decoupled so the contract is stable"]
S35["Backward compatibility — NotificationRepository / notification use cases / NotificationScreen / NotificationTile / EmptyNotification unchanged; every pre-Phase 48 widget keeps compiling; the unread-count badge in playground + profile keeps deriving from the same provider"]

