subgraph Phase51["Phase 51 — Backend Security (Implemented)"]

V1["firestore.rules — production-ready; helpers isSignedIn() / isOwner(uid) / isAdmin() / isPremium() / hasFields(data, fields); users/{uid} and every subcollection owner-only (request.auth.uid == userId)"]
V2["storage.rules — production-ready; users/{uid}/** owner-only + image/* + 5MB ceiling; premium/** premium-or-admin; content/** read-authenticated; default-deny catch-all"]
V3["firebase.json + firestore.indexes.json — rules + indexes + functions references + emulator ports; composite indexes for coin_ledger / leaderboard_entries / quiz_history / quiz_sessions / notifications / bookmarks / notes"]
V4["RoleGuard (lib/core/security/role_guard.dart) — enum SecurityAction { readOwn, writeOwn, readPublic, mutateAdmin, mutatePremium }; static hasRole / requiredRole / assertAuthorized / assertOwnership"]
V5["AuthorizationException extends AppException — carries action + requiredRole + actualRole; ErrorHandler.map translates to the existing AuthorizationFailure"]
V6["securityContextProvider (lib/core/security/security_context.dart) — Provider<UserEntity?> reads authStateProvider.user; null for guests"]
V7["isAuthenticatedProvider / isAdminProvider / isPremiumProvider — Provider<bool> shortcuts derived from securityContextProvider"]
V8["AuthGuard (lib/core/security/auth_precondition.dart) — composition over mixin (Ref captured in constructor); assertAuthenticated / assertAdmin / assertPremium / assertOwnership"]
V9["authStateResetProvider (lib/core/providers/auth_lifecycle.dart) — Provider<void> listens to authStateProvider; on logout (next.user == null) invalidates a hard-coded list of user-bound feature providers"]
V10["Registered providers in authStateResetDispatcherProvider: bookmarkControllerProvider, notesControllerProvider, notificationControllerProvider, profileControllerProvider, rewardsControllerProvider, streakControllerProvider, missionsControllerProvider, leaderboardControllerProvider, statisticsControllerProvider, aiHistoryControllerProvider, searchControllerProvider, subscriptionControllerProvider, syncControllerProvider, settingsControllerProvider"]
V11["AuthInterceptor (lib/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor.dart) — existing X-Require-Auth now rejects with 401 when currentUser == null (was silent no-op); new X-Require-Role header short-circuits with 403 when role mismatches; X-Force-Token-Refresh triggers user.getIdToken(true)"]
V12["AuthInterceptor.withRef(Ref ref) — Riverpod-aware constructor that resolves the active user / role for X-Require-Role checks; absent ref means role checks are best-effort skipped"]
V13["DioClient.build(secure: bool = false) — when true, AuthInterceptor is inserted BEFORE RetryInterceptor so 401 / 403 surface without retry storms; default X-Require-Auth: true is added to every request"]
V14["SecureDioClient.build({baseUrl, ref, extraInterceptors}) — wraps DioClient.build(secure: true, authInterceptor: AuthInterceptor.withRef(ref), defaultHeaders: {X-Require-Auth: 'true', X-Require-Role: 'authenticated'}); Cloud Function callers get auth + role by default"]
V15["Repository security — bookmark / notes / notification / profile / ai_tutor / quiz_engine / review / search / settings / offline repositories capture a Riverpod Ref in their constructor and call _guard.assertAuthenticated() at the top of every mutating method"]
V16["Quiz Hub stays public — quiz_api_repository_impl.dart is intentionally unchanged; docs/apidoc/api documents the Quiz Hub REST API as 'No auth required'; Phase 51 does not add auth to Quiz Hub calls"]
V17["firestore.rules public content collections — categories / subjects / chapters / lessons / mockTests / questions / achievements / rewards / gamificationState / leaderboardEntries: read = isSignedIn(), write = isAdmin()"]
V18["firestore.rules subscriptions + admin analytics — subscriptions read-owner / write-admin; adminLogs + analyticsEvents write-admin only; aiTutorLogs read-owner only (write denied; Cloud Functions own writes)"]
V19["firestore.rules coin ledger append-only — users/{uid}/coin_ledger/{txId} allows create when uid + source + sourceId + amount + createdAt are present; update + delete denied to preserve audit trail"]
V20["firestore.rules subcollection uid validation — create + update on quiz_sessions / quiz_history / coin_ledger / bookmarks / notes / highlights / ai_notes / notifications / fcm_tokens enforce request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid"]
V21["firestore.rules default-deny — catch-all match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if false(); } blocks unlisted paths"]
V22["storage.rules users/{uid}/{allPaths=**} — read + write only when request.auth.uid == uid; uploads restricted to image/jpeg|png|webp, max 5 MB"]
V23["storage.rules premium/{allPaths=**} — read requires isPremiumOrAdmin() (Firestore role lookup); write-admin only"]
V24["storage.rules content/{allPaths=**} — read = isSignedIn(); write = isAdmin() (guidebook / lesson assets)"]
V25["Defence in depth — firestore.rules + storage.rules are the source of truth; AuthGuard / repository preconditions / SecureDioClient are client-side layered checks; a malicious client cannot bypass server-side enforcement"]
V26["Guest guard (client-side) — every AuthGuard.assertAuthenticated() call returns AuthorizationFailure when the active user is null; local cache still mirrors in-session actions; Firestore writes are gated; matches the existing service-level uid.isEmpty short-circuits"]
V27["Provider reset on logout — authStateResetProvider fires whenever authStateProvider transitions to AuthState.unauthenticated(); every registered provider is invalidated; no stale user data leaks across accounts"]
V28["Backward compatibility — no UI redesign; all existing repositories, services, providers, controllers, widgets stay valid; new constructor parameters (ref: ref) are additive"]
V29["Failure vocabulary unchanged — AuthorizationFailure (existing in failures.dart) handles every denial path; no new Failure type added; AuthorizationException integrates via ErrorHandler.map"]
V30["Phase 52 follow-ups — firestore.isAdmin() reads users/{uid}/role (doc lookup, not custom claim); Phase 52 will migrate to setCustomUserClaims + token refresh for production"]

